        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF149 Allow more characters in DOM APIs]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29217</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29217"/>
        <updated>2026-03-23T01:53:52.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF149 adds support for additional characters to be allowed in attribute and element names in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1773312" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1773312</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Previously  you could only use the chars allowed in XML names - now the rules are less restrictive to allow the same chars as the HTML parser.</p>
<p dir="auto">Spec update: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1263558481" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7991" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/whatwg/html/pull/7991/hovercard" href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7991">whatwg/html#7991</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Chrome states support in 143:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-143-beta#allow_more_characters_in_javascript_dom_apis" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-143-beta#allow_more_characters_in_javascript_dom_apis</a></li>
<li><a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/6278918763708416" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6278918763708416</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Webkit added support in <a href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=241419" rel="nofollow">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=241419</a>  but I don't think this made it to Safari yet.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3978124831" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43218" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43218/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43218">mdn/content#43218</a></p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>hamishwillee</name>
            <email>hamishwillee@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/hamishwillee</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-03-10T04:29:38.000Z</published>
    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Chrome 146 / Safari 26 add `createElement` option `customElementRegistry`]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29216</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29216"/>
        <updated>2026-03-24T00:36:58.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">There is a new option <code class="notranslate">customElementRegistry</code> to the <code class="notranslate">options</code> parameter that can be passed to <code class="notranslate">Document.createElement()</code> or <code class="notranslate">Document.createElementNS()</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">According to <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/blog/scoped-registries?hl=en#scope_to_an_individual_element" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/scoped-registries?hl=en#scope_to_an_individual_element</a> support was added in Chrome 146 and Safari 26 - that seems likely for Safari from <a href="https://webkit.org/blog/17674/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-234/" rel="nofollow">https://webkit.org/blog/17674/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-234/</a> and from the related APIs such as <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CustomElementRegistry/CustomElementRegistry" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CustomElementRegistry/CustomElementRegistry</a></p>
<p dir="auto">This adds both an <code class="notranslate">options.customElementRegistry</code> and <code class="notranslate">options.is</code> parameter to the two methods. The assumption is that <code class="notranslate">is</code> was supported in Chrome from start (seems likely), and from Safari in 26. I can't see information confirming this for Safari, but I think it likely.</p>
<p dir="auto">Note, no evidence Firefox supports either yet.</p>
<p dir="auto">This fell out of work being done for</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3978124831" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43218" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43218/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43218">mdn/content#43218</a></li>
</ul>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>hamishwillee</name>
            <email>hamishwillee@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/hamishwillee</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-03-10T00:52:01.000Z</published>
    </entry>
